* ============================================================================
* CD74HC4066 - one channel of the quad bilateral switch, behavioural model (2026-09-29)
* Not a TI model.  Values from TI's CD74HC4066 data sheet SCHS208E (July 2024), read 2026-09-29:
*   on-resistance, VCC 4.5 V, 1 mA ..... 25 ohm typ (80 max) with the signal at a rail, 35 ohm typ (95 max) mid-range
*                                        -> RON = 25: on the board the switch carries the ~0.16 V servo input
*   control input ...................... HC CMOS levels (VIH 3.15 V, VIL 1.35 V at 4.5 V); smooth threshold at VDD/2
*   switch turn-on / turn-off delay .... max 20 / 30 ns at 4.5 V, about 10 ns typ at 5 V  -> TON (one RC for both)
*   off-state leakage .................. max 0.1 uA at 25 C, 1 uA over -55 to 85 C (not modelled: 10 GOhm when off)
* Pins: A B CTRL VDD VSS.  CTRL high = switch closed.
* NOT MODELLED: Ron change with signal voltage, charge injection, channel capacitances, leakage.
* ============================================================================
.SUBCKT CD74HC4066 A B CTRL VDD VSS PARAMS: RON=25 ROFF=10G TON=10n
BC c1 VSS V=0.5+0.5*tanh((V(CTRL,VSS)-0.5*V(VDD,VSS))/0.05)
RD c1 c2 1k
CD c2 VSS {TON/0.69/1k}
BS A B I=V(A,B)*(min(max(V(c2,VSS),0),1)/RON+1/ROFF)
RIN CTRL VSS 1G
.ENDS CD74HC4066
